                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "749fb5ce-fff0-341c-9fce-10db2929ef92",
                        "entry_id": "79f565f1-b974-3b7c-a499-cc2a1dc2582b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Staatsbürger des Senegal"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d34693c0-f12d-4286-b189-eff1b5e9dbbc",
                                "sense_id": "749fb5ce-fff0-341c-9fce-10db2929ef92",
                                "text": "„Monsieur Desgranges’ Urgroßvater hatte Glasperlen eingekauft, war damit nach Senegal gefahren, um sie dort gegen Senegalesen einzutauschen.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f47b4bbd-f10d-40db-83f7-85e223c4076e",
                        "source_entry_id": "79f565f1-b974-3b7c-a499-cc2a1dc2582b",
                        "source_sense_id": "749fb5ce-fff0-341c-9fce-10db2929ef92",
                        "source_sense_description": "Staatsbürger des Senegal",
                        "target_lang_word": "Senegalese",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Senegalese",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "473a8b85-ddea-3279-9c3b-3bf891d25064",
                                        "entry_id": "c6bc362f-c33c-32e4-886d-8671af500a45",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, from, or pertaining to Senegal or the Senegalese people."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Senegalese",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a2b150a-33bd-3e0a-8b79-692fcd87ab8e",
                                        "entry_id": "826dc43f-c4f7-3ce4-985d-bb65e0076218",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person from Senegal or of Senegalese descent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in-plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80b97caf-4716-48bd-8706-320ea3720165",
                                                "sense_id": "2a2b150a-33bd-3e0a-8b79-692fcd87ab8e",
                                                "text": "Foreigner who marries a Senegalese is granted permanent residency and can apply for citizenship by naturalization."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d4620b2-c9a4-4293-a2ea-118880ed8f21",
                                                "sense_id": "2a2b150a-33bd-3e0a-8b79-692fcd87ab8e",
                                                "text": "In times of need, it is the mother's brother whom a Senegalese is most likely to approach for aid. The matrilineage is dominated by the tokor (\"tuh-CORE\"), the oldest man. The tokor holds all the family money."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3865953c-c2ed-4264-87c6-312c1a90828c",
                                                "sense_id": "2a2b150a-33bd-3e0a-8b79-692fcd87ab8e",
                                                "text": "Senghor writes that these texts were collected “by the Abbé Boilat, a Senegalese” in his Grammar of the Wolof Language. Identifying Boilat as “a Senegalese” conflicts with the more ambiguous ways that Boilat actually presents himself[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4e81e91f-c7d9-4171-a495-3c600f35941e",
                        "source_entry_id": "79f565f1-b974-3b7c-a499-cc2a1dc2582b",
                        "source_sense_id": "749fb5ce-fff0-341c-9fce-10db2929ef92",
                        "source_sense_description": "Staatsbürger des Senegal",
                        "target_lang_word": "Sénégalais",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Sénégalais",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2d513ac-32af-3918-83b2-8280b5721e85",
                                        "entry_id": "852e9ab7-0de0-3cbf-8c30-1c91b2b27ca8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne du Sénégal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21489173-5308-4442-a544-e29c5fd39bb1",
                                                "sense_id": "c2d513ac-32af-3918-83b2-8280b5721e85",
                                                "text": "Les deux Sénégalais, chéchia rouge en arrière de leur crâne luisant de sueur, tournaient mélancoliquement dans la pièce, à l’affût d’ordres que personne ne leur donnait."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9e4568d-5ab8-4c1b-aa9f-ff148fc893cd",
                                                "sense_id": "c2d513ac-32af-3918-83b2-8280b5721e85",
                                                "text": "Les tirailleurs de l’escouade qui venait de lui rendre les honneurs se dispersèrent. Il y avait là une douzaine de Sénégalais pur sang : Ouolofs à la barbe en collier, aux mollets grêles, Malinkés, Sérères, Bambaras aux joues barrées de trois balafres verticales."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89873c57-f621-43c5-94b1-f3bdd33df1f0",
                                                "sense_id": "c2d513ac-32af-3918-83b2-8280b5721e85",
                                                "text": "Seule la France l’a effectivement fait à travers le Programme développement local migration (PDLM), conçu essentiellement pour accompagner les IQF (Invitations à quitter le territoire français) des Maliens et Sénégalais (les plus nombreux à être reconduits à la frontière)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "689519f8-aa2f-4642-a374-43e231e1b1dc",
                        "source_entry_id": "79f565f1-b974-3b7c-a499-cc2a1dc2582b",
                        "source_sense_id": "749fb5ce-fff0-341c-9fce-10db2929ef92",
